{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# DC segmenting Markdown to wiki renderer\n\n## Problem and boundaries\nJira Data Center stores wiki markup while rebar authors Markdown. DC sends Markdown literally. Whole-body pandoc 3.6.1 was measured to escape prose/code arrows, erode tables, and delete the <!-- rebar:reconciler-echo --> marker.\n\nAdd an unwired pure renderer. WikiTextCodec.fit_outbound retains 32,767-character truncation; normalize_outbound/to_wire stay identity; decode_inbound stays identity plus None-to-empty. OutboundFieldMapper, CREATE, normalize_rich_text, and live sends stay unchanged. Story 3388 owns cutover/echo suppression/convergence. Story 5c0e owns timeout/process/GPL/SBOM hardening. Cloud uses its ADF child.\n\nPandoc is chosen because its maintained CommonMark/Jira pair produced 98.4% eligible-character coverage; surveyed md-to-jira, mistune-jira, and md-jira lack equivalent maintained Jira-writer fidelity. Selective segmentation contains measured damage. ADR 0083 governs imports. Add ADR 0095 plus docs/adr/.numbers/0095 for decision, invariants, pin provenance, alternatives, platform boundary, and deferrals.\n\n## Corpus\nCommit a deterministic scrubbed sample from scripts/build_dc_wiki_corpus.py: 29 code-arrow, 29 table, and 120 prose bodies (178 total). The fixed-seed generator scrubs before writing, covers each available protected phenomenon plus prose, and keeps shards below 500 KB.\n\nRecords declare source, protected excerpts, and eligible safe units independently of renderer output. Exclude tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus in scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py. Reject emails, tenant hostnames, and URLs.\n\nBody ratio = bodies with a changed eligible safe unit / 178. Character ratio = source characters in changed eligible units / source characters in all eligible units. The exact pin measured 0.927/0.984; tests require >=0.90/>=0.95. Identity fallback fails because eligible outputs must differ.\n\n## Renderer contract\nAdd adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py with render_markdown_to_wiki(markdown: str) -> str.\n\nTwo-phase left-to-right lexer:\n1. Lock complete {noformat} spans, backtick/tilde fences, and four-space-indented blocks, including internal blank lines.\n2. Split intervening text into blank-line blocks plus list items; preserve separators/order.\n\nClassify:\n1. Locked blocks plus units beginning h1.-h6., {code}, {noformat}, or {{ pass exactly.\n2. ASCII table = >=2 pipe-bearing lines with a pipes/colons/hyphens/whitespace delimiter row. Wrap exact bytes once in {noformat}.\n3. HTML comment or tag matching <[/!]?[A-Za-z][^>]*> passes exactly.\n4. Prose outside extracted code containing (?; \\b/\\d/\\s/\\w; or a bracket class followed by *, +, ?, or {n,m} passes exactly.\n5. Remaining headings, quotes, list items, and prose render via pypandoc commonmark -> jira with --wrap=none.\n\nCode fragments are fences, four-space blocks, and inline spans delimited by matching backtick runs. Extract/mask them before classifiers 3-4 plus arrow substitution. In safe units make one regex pass ordered <!--, -->, <->, ->, <-, =>. Map arrows to ↔/→/←/⇒; both HTML delimiters always map to themselves, including prose -->. Sequential replacement is forbidden. Inline code copies exactly.\n\nEvery extracted fragment must appear byte-identically in order after conversion; otherwise return that source unit. Strip pandoc's content-free {anchor:} after headings. Existing wiki stays exact over repeated rendering.\n\nMissing pypandoc returns the body with a content-free structured warning. Conversion/preservation failure returns that unit with a content-free structured debug fallback class. Module state is immutable.\n\n## Dependency and CI\nAdd wiki = [\"pypandoc-binary==1.15\"] plus wiki in dev. Register wiki in rebar._optional.EXTRAS with pypandoc probe; regenerate uv.lock. In .github/workflows/_optionality.yml add wiki:wiki, remove stale eval:eval, and change union:agents,eval,tracing to union:agents,tracing,wiki. Existing parity/removed-eval tests stay green.\n\nAn exact-pin probe reports pypandoc 1.15, pandoc 3.6.1, and commonmark-to-jira output. A non-skipping test hard-imports pypandoc, requires 3.6.1, then proves the jira writer with an exact heading conversion (not get_pandoc_formats). Wiki tests never importorskip; dev installs wiki in project pytest lanes. Binary support covers project Linux/macOS CI plus Windows wheels; core/BSD keeps identity fallback. ADR 0095 records the boundary; story 5c0e owns hardening.\n\nChanged paths: src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py; scripts/build_dc_wiki_corpus.py; tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/; tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py; tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_corpus.py; pyproject.toml; uv.lock; src/rebar/_optional.py; .github/workflows/_optionality.yml; scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py; docs/adr/0095-dc-segmenting-wiki-renderer.md; docs/adr/.numbers/0095.\n\n## Verification\nAuthor the full oracle RED-first; collect without skip/xfail. Run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`, `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`, and `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make test`. Prove resolution with `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" uv sync --locked --extra wiki --extra agents --extra tracing`.\n\nNo contention test: stateless local transform; no store composition, retry/backoff, or cached state.\n\n## Surface parity\nCLI/MCP/API/public facade: out of scope. Automated callers plus dual-direction: story 3388. Cloud: ADF child.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Safe units render through real pandoc in order; test_dc_segmenting_passthrough.\n- [ ] Tables preserve exact bytes; test_dc_segmenting_passthrough.\n- [ ] HTML/regex-dangerous units preserve exact bytes; test_dc_segmenting_passthrough.\n- [ ] Specified arrows convert prose; test_arrow_substitution_cases.\n- [ ] Code arrows stay exact; prose/code --> stays exact; arrow tests.\n- [ ] All 29 code-arrow fixtures retain protected excerpts; corpus code-arrow test.\n- [ ] All 29 tables keep exact bytes inside one noformat wrapper over five passes; table tests.\n- [ ] HTML comments survive exactly; test_dc_corpus_html_comments_survive.\n- [ ] Existing wiki/noformat stays exact over five passes; idempotence tests.\n- [ ] Missing pandoc returns exact body; test_dc_pandoc_absent_identity.\n- [ ] Missing-pandoc warning contains no body; test_dc_pandoc_absent_identity.\n- [ ] Conversion/preservation failure returns exact unit; fallback test.\n- [ ] Failure log names only fallback class; fallback test.\n- [ ] wiki locks pypandoc-binary 1.15; packaging test.\n- [ ] wiki installs standalone plus jointly without removed eval; local uv sync plus optionality lane.\n- [ ] Real binary reports pandoc 3.6.1; test_dc_real_pandoc_version.\n- [ ] Real conversion proves jira heading output; test_dc_real_pandoc_version.\n- [ ] Rendered-body ratio >=0.90; test_dc_corpus_coverage.\n- [ ] Rendered-character ratio >=0.95 over eligible source; test_dc_corpus_coverage.\n- [ ] Cardinality = 29+29+120=178; test_corpus_cardinality_is_pinned.\n- [ ] Fixtures contain no email, tenant hostname, or URL; secrets test.\n- [ ] Heading output contains no content-free anchor; passthrough test.\n- [ ] ADR marker passes scripts/check_adr_numbers.py.\n- [ ] ADR contains Decision/Invariants/Dependency Pin/Alternatives/Deferred Boundaries; test_wiki_render.py.\n- [ ] Existing WikiTextCodec tests stay unmodified; make test."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786572238800940001,"uuid":"149b21f5-963c-4193-b686-cd4416217f6f"}